solution.text:
Li and $\mathrm{Mg}$ do not form solid bicarbonate, but react with $\mathrm{N}_{2}$ to give nitrides.

$\begin{array}{l}

6 \mathrm{Li}+\mathrm{N}_{2} \stackrel{\Delta}{\rightarrow} 2 \mathrm{Li}_{3} \mathrm{~N} \\

3 \mathrm{Mg}+\mathrm{N}_{2} \stackrel{\Delta}{\rightarrow} \mathrm{Mg}_{3} \mathrm{~N}_{2}

\end{array}$
